  "sourceData": {
    "answer": "to: {drift/float} | {waft-(e.g.-a-scent)/hang-in-the-air} | be-in-the-air-(e.g.-a-feeling-or-mood) | {wander/walk-around-aimlessly} | be-{unsteady/unstable} | {falter/flinch/wince} | live-in-unreliable-circumstances",
    "mnemonic": "Because the hiragana ends with an <ja>う</ja> sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means <kanji>drift</kanji> and the verb vocab version is <vocabulary>to drift</vocabulary> or <vocabulary>to waft</vocabulary>.",
    "readingMnemonic": "You're going <vocabulary>to drift</vocabulary> away. Drifting drifting drifting. Then, you turn into a yo-yo and yell \"<reading>ta da yo</reading>-yo (<ja>ただよ</ja>)! Not sure why drifting turns you into a yo-yo, but imagine it and don't question it.",
